\c 11
\s1 The Broken Covenant
\p \v 1 \w This is the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w from the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*: \v 2 “\w Listen|strong="H8085"\w* \w to the words|strong="H1697"\w* \w of this|strong="H2063"\w* \w covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w and tell them|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w and the residents|strong="H3427"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*. \v 3 \w You must tell them that|strong="H559"\w* \w this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w Cursed is|strong="H779"\w* \w the man|strong="H376"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w does not|strong="H3808"\w* \w obey|strong="H8085"\w* \w the words|strong="H1697"\w* \w of this|strong="H2063"\w* \w covenant|strong="H1285"\w*, \v 4 \w which|strong="H834"\w* \w I commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w your forefathers|strong="H1"\w* \w when|strong="H3117"\w* \w I brought them out|strong="H3318"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*, \w out of the iron|strong="H1270"\w* \w furnace|strong="H3564"\w*, \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w Obey Me|strong="H8085"\w*, \w and do|strong="H6213"\w* \w everything|strong="H3605"\w* \w I command you|strong="H6680"\w*, \w and you will be|strong="H1961"\w* My \w people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w and I|strong="H595"\w* \w will be|strong="H1961"\w* your \w God|strong="H430"\w*.’ \v 5 \w This was in order to|strong="H4616"\w* \w establish|strong="H6965"\w* \w the oath|strong="H7621"\w* \w I swore|strong="H7650"\w* \w to your forefathers|strong="H1"\w*, \w to give them|strong="H5414"\w* \w a land|strong="H776"\w* \w flowing|strong="H2100"\w* \w with milk|strong="H2461"\w* \w and honey|strong="H1706"\w*, \w as it is to this day|strong="H3117"\w*.”
