\c 19
\s1 The Broken Jar
\p \v 1 \w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: “\w Go|strong="H1980"\w* \w and buy|strong="H7069"\w* \w a clay|strong="H2789"\w* \w jar|strong="H1228"\w* \w from a potter|strong="H3335"\w*. \w Take some of the elders|strong="H2205"\w* \w of the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w and leaders|strong="H2205"\w* \w of the priests|strong="H3548"\w*, \v 2 \w and go|strong="H3318"\w* \w out to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Valley|strong="H1516"\w* \w of Ben-hinnom|strong="H1121"\w* \w near the entrance|strong="H6607"\w* \w of the Potsherd|strong="H2777"\w* \w Gate|strong="H8179"\w*.
\p \w Proclaim|strong="H7121"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w* \w the words|strong="H1697"\w* \w I speak|strong="H1696"\w* \w to you|strong="H413"\w*, \v 3 \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w Hear|strong="H8085"\w* \w the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w O kings|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w and residents|strong="H3427"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*. \w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H6635"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w I am going to bring|strong="H935"\w* \w such disaster|strong="H7451"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w the ears|strong="H241"\w* \w of all|strong="H3605"\w* \w who hear of it|strong="H8085"\w* \w will ring|strong="H6750"\w*, \v 4 \w because|strong="H3282"\w* \w they have abandoned Me|strong="H5800"\w* \w and made this|strong="H2088"\w* \w a foreign|strong="H5234"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w*. \w They have burned incense|strong="H6999"\w* in this place \w to other|strong="H312"\w* \w gods|strong="H430"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w neither they|strong="H1992"\w* \w nor their fathers|strong="H1"\w* \w nor the kings|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w have ever|strong="H3808"\w* \w known|strong="H3045"\w*. \w They have filled|strong="H4390"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w with the blood|strong="H1818"\w* \w of the innocent|strong="H5355"\w*. \v 5 \w They have built|strong="H1129"\w* \w high places|strong="H1116"\w* \w to Baal|strong="H1168"\w* \w on which to burn|strong="H8313"\w* \w their children|strong="H1121"\w* \w in the fire|strong="H784"\w* \w as offerings|strong="H5930"\w* \w to Baal|strong="H1168"\w* — \w something|strong="H834"\w* \w I never|strong="H3808"\w* \w commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w or mentioned|strong="H1696"\w*, \w nor|strong="H3808"\w* \w did it even enter|strong="H5927"\w* \w My mind|strong="H3820"\w*.
\p \v 6 \w So|strong="H3651"\w* \w behold|strong="H2009"\w*, \w the days|strong="H3117"\w* \w are coming|strong="H935"\w*, \w declares|strong="H5002"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w when this|strong="H2088"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w will no|strong="H3808"\w* \w longer|strong="H5750"\w* \w be called|strong="H7121"\w* \w Topheth|strong="H8612"\w* \w or the Valley|strong="H1516"\w* \w of Ben-hinnom|strong="H1121"\w*, \w but|strong="H3588"\w* \w the Valley|strong="H1516"\w* \w of Slaughter|strong="H2028"\w*. \v 7 \w And in this|strong="H2088"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w I will ruin|strong="H1238"\w*\f + \fr 19:7 \ft The Hebrew term for \fqa ruin \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa jar\ft ; see verses 1 and 10.\f* \w the plans|strong="H6098"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w and Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*. \w I will make them fall|strong="H5307"\w* \w by the sword|strong="H2719"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w their enemies|strong="H341"\w*, \w by the hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w of those who seek|strong="H1245"\w* \w their lives|strong="H5315"\w*, \w and I will give|strong="H5414"\w* \w their carcasses|strong="H5038"\w* \w as food|strong="H3978"\w* \w to the birds|strong="H5775"\w* \w of the air|strong="H8064"\w* \w and the beasts|strong="H929"\w* \w of the earth|strong="H776"\w*.
\p \v 8 \w I will make|strong="H7760"\w* \w this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w a desolation|strong="H8047"\w* \w and an object of scorn|strong="H8322"\w*.\f + \fr 19:8 \ft Literally \fqa and a hissing\f* \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w who pass|strong="H5674"\w* \w by|strong="H5921"\w* \w will be appalled|strong="H8074"\w* \w and will scoff|strong="H8319"\w* \w at|strong="H5921"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w her wounds|strong="H4347"\w*. \v 9 \w I will make them eat|strong="H398"\w* \w the flesh|strong="H1320"\w* \w of their sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w daughters|strong="H1323"\w*, \w and they will eat|strong="H398"\w* \w one|strong="H376"\w* \w another’s|strong="H7453"\w* \w flesh|strong="H1320"\w* \w in the siege|strong="H4692"\w* \w and distress|strong="H4689"\w* \w inflicted|strong="H6693"\w* on them \w by their enemies|strong="H341"\w* \w who seek|strong="H1245"\w* \w their lives|strong="H5315"\w*.’
\p \v 10 \w Then you are to shatter|strong="H7665"\w* \w the jar|strong="H1228"\w* \w in the presence|strong="H5869"\w* \w of the men|strong="H582"\w* \w who accompany|strong="H1980"\w* \w you|strong="H854"\w*, \v 11 \w and you are to proclaim|strong="H559"\w* \w to them|strong="H413"\w* \w that this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H6635"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w I will shatter|strong="H7665"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w nation|strong="H5971"\w* \w and this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w like|strong="H834"\w* \w one shatters|strong="H7665"\w* \w a potter’s|strong="H3335"\w* \w jar|strong="H3627"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w can|strong="H3201"\w* \w never|strong="H3808"\w* \w again|strong="H5750"\w* \w be repaired|strong="H7495"\w*. \w They will bury the dead|strong="H6912"\w* \w in Topheth|strong="H8612"\w* \w until there is no more|strong="H369"\w* \w room|strong="H4725"\w* \w to bury them|strong="H6912"\w*.
