\c 21
\s1 Jerusalem Will Fall to Babylon
\p \v 1 \w This is the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w from|strong="H854"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w when King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w* \w to him|strong="H413"\w* \w Pashhur|strong="H6583"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Malchijah|strong="H4441"\w* \w and the priest|strong="H3548"\w* \w Zephaniah|strong="H6846"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Maaseiah|strong="H4641"\w*. \w They said|strong="H559"\w*, \v 2 “\w Please|strong="H4994"\w* \w inquire|strong="H1875"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w on our behalf|strong="H1157"\w*, \w since|strong="H3588"\w* \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w*\f + \fr 21:2 \ft Hebrew \fqa Nebuchadrezzar\ft , a variant of \fqa Nebuchadnezzar \ft (king of Babylon), which occurs frequently in Jeremiah. The latter spelling is used throughout Jeremiah for consistency.\f* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w is waging war|strong="H3898"\w* \w against us|strong="H5921"\w*. \w Perhaps|strong="H194"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w will perform|strong="H6213"\w* \w for us|strong="H854"\w* \w something like all|strong="H3605"\w* \w His past wonders|strong="H6381"\w*, \w so that Nebuchadnezzar will withdraw|strong="H5927"\w* \w from us|strong="H5921"\w*.”
\p \v 3 \w But Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w answered|strong="H559"\w*, “\w You are to tell|strong="H559"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w that|strong="H3541"\w* \v 4 \w this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w says|strong="H559"\w*: ‘\w I will turn|strong="H5437"\w* \w against you|strong="H853"\w* \w the weapons|strong="H3627"\w* \w of war|strong="H4421"\w* \w in your hands|strong="H3027"\w*, \w with which|strong="H834"\w* \w you|strong="H859"\w* \w are fighting|strong="H3898"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w and the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*\f + \fr 21:4 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verse 9\f* \w who besiege|strong="H6696"\w* \w you|strong="H5921"\w* \w outside|strong="H2351"\w* \w the wall|strong="H2346"\w*, \w and I will assemble|strong="H622"\w* \w their forces|strong="H853"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w the center|strong="H8432"\w* \w of this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w*. \v 5 \w And I Myself|strong="H589"\w* \w will fight|strong="H3898"\w* \w against you|strong="H854"\w* \w with an outstretched|strong="H5186"\w* \w hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w and a mighty|strong="H2389"\w* \w arm|strong="H2220"\w*, \w with anger|strong="H639"\w*, \w fury|strong="H2534"\w*, \w and great|strong="H1419"\w* \w wrath|strong="H7110"\w*. \v 6 \w I will strike down|strong="H5221"\w* \w the residents|strong="H3427"\w* \w of this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w both man|strong="H120"\w* \w and beast|strong="H929"\w*. \w They will die|strong="H4191"\w* \w in a terrible|strong="H1419"\w* \w plague|strong="H1698"\w*.’
\p \v 7 ‘\w After that|strong="H310"\w*,’ \w declares|strong="H5002"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, ‘\w I will hand over|strong="H5414"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*, \w his officers|strong="H5650"\w*, \w and the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w in this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w who survive|strong="H7604"\w* \w the plague|strong="H1698"\w* \w and sword|strong="H2719"\w* \w and famine|strong="H7458"\w*, \w to|strong="H3027"\w* \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w and to|strong="H3027"\w* \w their enemies|strong="H341"\w* \w who seek|strong="H1245"\w* \w their lives|strong="H5315"\w*. \w He will put them|strong="H5221"\w* \w to the sword|strong="H2719"\w*; \w he will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w spare|strong="H2347"\w* \w them|strong="H5921"\w* \w or|strong="H3808"\w* \w show pity|strong="H2550"\w* \w or|strong="H3808"\w* \w compassion|strong="H7355"\w*.’
\p \v 8 \w Furthermore, you are to tell|strong="H559"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w people|strong="H5971"\w* \w that this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: ‘\w Behold|strong="H2005"\w*, \w I set|strong="H5414"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w you|strong="H853"\w* \w the way|strong="H1870"\w* \w of life|strong="H2416"\w* \w and the way|strong="H1870"\w* \w of death|strong="H4194"\w*. \v 9 \w Whoever stays|strong="H3427"\w* \w in this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w will die|strong="H4191"\w* \w by sword|strong="H2719"\w* \w and famine|strong="H7458"\w* \w and plague|strong="H1698"\w*, \w but whoever goes out|strong="H3318"\w* \w and surrenders|strong="H5307"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w* \w who besiege|strong="H6696"\w* \w you|strong="H5921"\w* \w will live|strong="H2421"\w*; \w he will retain|strong="H1961"\w* his \w life|strong="H5315"\w* \w like a spoil of war|strong="H7998"\w*. \v 10 \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w I have set|strong="H7760"\w* \w My face|strong="H6440"\w* \w against this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w to bring disaster|strong="H7451"\w* \w and not|strong="H3808"\w* \w good|strong="H2896"\w*, \w declares|strong="H5002"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \w It will be delivered|strong="H5414"\w* \w into the hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w who will destroy it|strong="H8313"\w* \w with fire|strong="H784"\w*.’
\s1 A Message to the House of David
\p \v 11 \w Moreover, tell the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w to hear|strong="H8085"\w* \w the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \v 12 \w O house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of David|strong="H1732"\w*, \w this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\w Administer|strong="H1777"\w* \w justice every morning|strong="H4941"\w*,
\q2 \w and rescue|strong="H5337"\w* \w the victim of robbery|strong="H1497"\w*
