\c 27
\s1 The Yoke of Nebuchadnezzar
\p \v 1 \w At the beginning|strong="H7225"\w* \w of the reign|strong="H4467"\w* \w of Zedekiah|strong="H3079"\w*\f + \fr 27:1 \ft A few Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac (see also verses 3 and 12, and \ref Jeremiah 28:1|JER 28:1\ref*); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Jehoiakim\f* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Josiah|strong="H2977"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*, \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w word|strong="H1697"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w from the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.\f + \fr 27:1 \ft Most LXX manuscripts do not include this verse.\f* \v 2 \w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to me|strong="H413"\w*:
