\p \v 12 \w And to|strong="H413"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w I spoke|strong="H1696"\w* \w the same|strong="H3605"\w* \w message|strong="H1697"\w*: “\w Put|strong="H935"\w* \w your necks|strong="H6677"\w* \w under the yoke|strong="H5923"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*; \w serve|strong="H5647"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w and his people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w and live|strong="H2421"\w*! \v 13 \w Why|strong="H4100"\w* \w should you|strong="H859"\w* \w and your people|strong="H5971"\w* \w die|strong="H4191"\w* \w by sword|strong="H2719"\w* \w and famine|strong="H7458"\w* \w and plague|strong="H1698"\w*, \w as|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has decreed|strong="H1696"\w* \w against|strong="H413"\w* \w any nation|strong="H1471"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w does not|strong="H3808"\w* \w serve|strong="H5647"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*?
