\s1 Hananiah’s False Prophecy
\p \v 1 \w In the fifth|strong="H2549"\w* \w month|strong="H2320"\w* \w of that same|strong="H1931"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w*, \w the fourth|strong="H7243"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w*, \w near the beginning|strong="H7225"\w* \w of the reign|strong="H4467"\w* \w of King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*, \w the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w Hananiah|strong="H2608"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Azzur|strong="H5809"\w*, \w who was from Gibeon|strong="H1391"\w*, \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to me|strong="H413"\w* \w in the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w in the presence|strong="H5869"\w* \w of the priests|strong="H3548"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*: \v 2 “\w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H6635"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w says|strong="H559"\w*: ‘\w I have broken|strong="H7665"\w* \w the yoke|strong="H5923"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*. \v 3 \w Within two years|strong="H8141"\w* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w will restore|strong="H7725"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the articles|strong="H3627"\w* \w of the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w removed|strong="H3947"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w here|strong="H2088"\w* \w and carried|strong="H935"\w* \w to Babylon|strong="H894"\w*. \v 4 \w And|strong="H853"\w* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w will restore|strong="H7725"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w Jeconiah|strong="H3204"\w*\f + \fr 28:4 \fqa Jeconiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoiachin\ft ; see \ref 2 Kings 24:12|2KI 24:12\ref*.\f* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Jehoiakim|strong="H3079"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*, \w along with|strong="H853"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the exiles|strong="H1546"\w* \w from Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w who went|strong="H935"\w* \w to Babylon|strong="H894"\w*,’ \w declares|strong="H5002"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, ‘\w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w I will break|strong="H7665"\w* \w the yoke|strong="H5923"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*.’”
\p \v 5 \w Then the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w Hananiah|strong="H2608"\w* \w in the presence|strong="H5869"\w* \w of the priests|strong="H3548"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w who were standing|strong="H5975"\w* \w in the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. \v 6 “\w Amen|strong="H543"\w*!” \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w*. “\w May the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w do|strong="H6213"\w* \w so|strong="H3651"\w*! \w May the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w fulfill|strong="H6965"\w* \w the words|strong="H1697"\w* \w you have prophesied|strong="H5012"\w*, \w and may He restore|strong="H7725"\w* \w the articles|strong="H3627"\w* \w of His|strong="H3068"\w* \w house|strong="H1004"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the exiles|strong="H1473"\w* \w back|strong="H413"\w* \w to this|strong="H2088"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w from Babylon|strong="H894"\w*.
\p \v 7 \w Nevertheless|strong="H389"\w*, \w listen|strong="H8085"\w* \w now|strong="H4994"\w* \w to this|strong="H2088"\w* \w message|strong="H1697"\w* \w I|strong="H595"\w* \w am speaking|strong="H1696"\w* \w in your hearing|strong="H241"\w* \w and in the hearing|strong="H241"\w* \w of all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*. \v 8 \w The prophets|strong="H5030"\w* \w of old|strong="H5769"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w preceded|strong="H1961"\w* \w you|strong="H4480"\w* \w and me|strong="H6440"\w* \w prophesied|strong="H5012"\w* \w war|strong="H4421"\w*, \w disaster|strong="H7451"\w*, \w and plague|strong="H1698"\w* \w against|strong="H413"\w* \w many|strong="H7227"\w* \w lands|strong="H776"\w* \w and great|strong="H1419"\w* \w kingdoms|strong="H4467"\w*. \v 9 \w As for the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w prophesies|strong="H5012"\w* \w peace|strong="H7965"\w*, \w only if the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w comes true|strong="H935"\w* \w will the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w be recognized|strong="H3045"\w* \w as one the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has truly|strong="H571"\w* \w sent|strong="H7971"\w*.”
