\q2 \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w I have spoken|strong="H1696"\w*
\q1 \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*
\q2 \w and the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*.
\q1 \v 15 \w In those|strong="H1992"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w and at that|strong="H1931"\w* \w time|strong="H6256"\w*
\q2 \w I will cause to sprout|strong="H6779"\w* \w for David|strong="H1732"\w* \w a righteous|strong="H6666"\w* \w Branch|strong="H6780"\w*,
\q1 \w and He will administer|strong="H6213"\w* \w justice|strong="H4941"\w*
\q2 \w and righteousness|strong="H6666"\w* \w in the land|strong="H776"\w*.
\q1 \v 16 \w In those|strong="H1992"\w* \w days|strong="H3117"\w* \w Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w will be saved|strong="H3467"\w*,
\q2 \w and Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w will dwell securely|strong="H7931"\w*,
\q1 \w and this|strong="H2088"\w* \w is the name|strong="H834"\w* \w by which it will be called|strong="H7121"\w*:
\q2 \w The LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w Our Righteousness|strong="H6664"\w*.\f + \fr 33:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa YHWH Tsidqenu\f*
\p \v 17 \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w will never|strong="H3808"\w* \w lack|strong="H3772"\w* \w a man|strong="H376"\w* \w to sit|strong="H3427"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w the throne|strong="H3678"\w* \w of the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \v 18 \w nor|strong="H3808"\w* \w will the priests|strong="H3548"\w* \w who are Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w ever|strong="H3605"\w* \w fail|strong="H3772"\w* \w to have a man|strong="H376"\w* \w before Me|strong="H6440"\w* \w to offer|strong="H5927"\w* \w burnt offerings|strong="H5930"\w*, \w to burn|strong="H6999"\w* \w grain offerings|strong="H4503"\w*, \w and to present|strong="H6213"\w* \w sacrifices|strong="H2077"\w*.”
\p \v 19 \w And the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*: \v 20 “\w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w If|strong="H518"\w* \w you can break|strong="H6565"\w* \w My covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w with the day|strong="H3117"\w* \w and My covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w with the night|strong="H3915"\w*, \w so that day|strong="H3119"\w* \w and night|strong="H3915"\w* \w cease|strong="H1115"\w* \w to occupy|strong="H1961"\w* \w their appointed time|strong="H6256"\w*, \v 21 \w then My covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w may also|strong="H1571"\w* \w be broken|strong="H6565"\w* \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w My servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w and with|strong="H854"\w* \w My ministers|strong="H8334"\w* \w the Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w who are priests|strong="H3548"\w*, \w so that David will not have|strong="H1961"\w* \w a son|strong="H1121"\w* \w to reign|strong="H4427"\w* \w on|strong="H5921"\w* \w his throne|strong="H3678"\w*. \v 22 \w As|strong="H834"\w* \w the hosts|strong="H6635"\w* \w of heaven|strong="H8064"\w* \w cannot|strong="H3808"\w* \w be counted|strong="H5608"\w* \w and as the sand|strong="H2344"\w* \w on the seashore|strong="H3220"\w* \w cannot|strong="H3808"\w* \w be measured|strong="H4058"\w*, \w so too|strong="H3651"\w* \w will I multiply|strong="H7235"\w* \w the descendants|strong="H2233"\w* \w of My servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w* \w and the Levites|strong="H3881"\w* \w who minister|strong="H8334"\w* \w before Me|strong="H853"\w*.”
\p \v 23 \w Moreover, the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*: \v 24 “\w Have you not|strong="H3808"\w* \w noticed|strong="H7200"\w* \w what|strong="H4100"\w* \w these|strong="H2088"\w* \w people|strong="H5971"\w* \w are saying|strong="H1696"\w*: ‘\w The LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has rejected|strong="H3988"\w* \w the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w families|strong="H4940"\w* \w He had chosen|strong="H977"\w*’? \w So they despise|strong="H5006"\w* \w My people|strong="H5971"\w* \w and no longer|strong="H5750"\w* \w regard them|strong="H1961"\w* \w as a nation|strong="H1471"\w*. \v 25 \w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w If|strong="H518"\w* \w I have not|strong="H3808"\w* \w established|strong="H7760"\w* \w My covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w with the day|strong="H3119"\w* \w and the night|strong="H3915"\w* \w and the fixed order|strong="H2708"\w* \w of heaven|strong="H8064"\w* \w and earth|strong="H776"\w*, \v 26 \w then I would also|strong="H1571"\w* \w reject|strong="H3988"\w* \w the descendants|strong="H2233"\w* \w of Jacob|strong="H3290"\w* \w and of My servant|strong="H5650"\w* \w David|strong="H1732"\w*, \w so as not to take|strong="H3947"\w* \w from his descendants|strong="H2233"\w* \w rulers|strong="H4910"\w* \w over|strong="H413"\w* \w the descendants|strong="H2233"\w* \w of Abraham|strong="H85"\w*, \w Isaac|strong="H3446"\w*, \w and Jacob|strong="H3290"\w*. \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w I will restore them|strong="H7725"\w* \w from captivity|strong="H7622"\w*\f + \fr 33:26 \ft Or \fqa restore their fortunes\f* \w and will have compassion on them|strong="H7355"\w*.”
\c 34
\s1 A Prophecy against Zedekiah
\p \v 1 \w This is the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w from the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w when Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w his army|strong="H2428"\w*, \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the earthly|strong="H776"\w* \w kingdoms|strong="H4467"\w* \w under his control|strong="H4475"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the other nations|strong="H5971"\w* \w were fighting|strong="H3898"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w its surrounding cities|strong="H5892"\w*. \v 2 \w The LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w told Jeremiah|strong="H559"\w* \w to go|strong="H1980"\w* \w and speak|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w and tell|strong="H559"\w* \w him|strong="H413"\w* \w that this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: “\w Behold|strong="H2005"\w*, \w I am about to deliver|strong="H5414"\w* \w this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w into the hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w and he will burn it down|strong="H8313"\w*. \v 3 \w And you yourself|strong="H859"\w* \w will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w escape|strong="H4422"\w* \w his grasp|strong="H3027"\w*, \w but|strong="H3588"\w* \w will surely be captured|strong="H8610"\w* \w and delivered|strong="H5414"\w* \w into his hand|strong="H3027"\w*. \w You will see|strong="H7200"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w eye|strong="H5869"\w* \w to eye|strong="H5869"\w* \w and speak with him|strong="H1696"\w* \w face|strong="H6310"\w* \w to|strong="H854"\w* \w face|strong="H6310"\w*; \w and you will go|strong="H935"\w* \w to Babylon|strong="H894"\w*.
\p \v 4 \w Yet|strong="H389"\w* \w hear|strong="H8085"\w* \w the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w O Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*. \w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w* \w concerning you|strong="H5921"\w*: \w You will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w die|strong="H4191"\w* \w by the sword|strong="H2719"\w*; \v 5 \w you will die|strong="H4191"\w* \w in peace|strong="H7965"\w*. \w As spices were burned|strong="H4955"\w* \w for your fathers|strong="H1"\w*, \w the former|strong="H7223"\w* \w kings|strong="H4428"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w preceded|strong="H1961"\w* \w you|strong="H6440"\w*, \w so|strong="H3651"\w* \w people will burn spices|strong="H8313"\w* for you \w and lament|strong="H5594"\w*, ‘\w Alas|strong="H1945"\w*, \w O master|strong="H113"\w*!’ \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w I Myself|strong="H589"\w* \w have spoken|strong="H1696"\w* \w this word|strong="H1697"\w*, \w declares|strong="H5002"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.”
\p \v 6 \w In Jerusalem, then|strong="H3389"\w*, \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w relayed|strong="H1696"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w these|strong="H428"\w* \w words|strong="H1697"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \v 7 \w as the army|strong="H2428"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w was fighting|strong="H3898"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w and the remaining|strong="H3498"\w* \w cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*— \w against|strong="H413"\w* \w Lachish|strong="H3923"\w* \w and Azekah|strong="H5825"\w*. \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w these were the only|strong="H2007"\w* \w fortified|strong="H4013"\w* \w cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w remaining|strong="H7604"\w* \w in Judah|strong="H3063"\w*.
\s1 Freedom for Hebrew Slaves
\p \v 8 \w After|strong="H310"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w had made|strong="H3772"\w* \w a covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w to proclaim|strong="H7121"\w* \w liberty|strong="H1865"\w*, \w the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w from|strong="H854"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \v 9 \w that each man|strong="H376"\w* \w should free|strong="H7971"\w* \w his Hebrew|strong="H5680"\w* \w slaves|strong="H5650"\w*, \w both male and female|strong="H5680"\w*, \w and no|strong="H1115"\w* \w one|strong="H376"\w* \w should hold|strong="H5647"\w* \w his fellow|strong="H251"\w* \w Jew in bondage|strong="H3064"\w*. \v 10 \w So all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w entered|strong="H935"\w* \w into this covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w agreed|strong="H8085"\w* \w that they would free|strong="H7971"\w* \w their menservants|strong="H5650"\w* \w and maidservants|strong="H8198"\w* \w and no longer|strong="H1115"\w* \w hold them in bondage|strong="H5647"\w*. \w They obeyed|strong="H8085"\w* \w and released them|strong="H7971"\w*, \v 11 \w but later|strong="H310"\w* \w they changed their minds|strong="H7725"\w* \w and took back|strong="H7725"\w* \w the menservants|strong="H5650"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w maidservants|strong="H8198"\w* \w they had freed|strong="H7971"\w*, \w and they forced them|strong="H3533"\w* \w to become slaves|strong="H5650"\w* \w again|strong="H8198"\w*.
\p \v 12 \w Then the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w from the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w saying|strong="H559"\w*, \v 13 “\w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w I|strong="H595"\w* \w made|strong="H3772"\w* \w a covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w your forefathers|strong="H1"\w* \w when|strong="H3117"\w* \w I brought them out|strong="H3318"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*, \w out of the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of slavery|strong="H5650"\w*, \w saying|strong="H559"\w*: \v 14 \w Every|strong="H7093"\w* \w seventh|strong="H7651"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w*, \w each|strong="H376"\w* \w of you must free|strong="H7971"\w* \w his Hebrew|strong="H5680"\w* \w brother|strong="H251"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w has sold himself|strong="H4376"\w* to you. \w He may serve|strong="H5647"\w* \w you six|strong="H8337"\w* \w years|strong="H8141"\w*, \w but then you must let him go|strong="H7971"\w* \w free|strong="H2670"\w*. \w But your fathers|strong="H1"\w* \w did not|strong="H3808"\w* \w listen|strong="H8085"\w* \w or incline|strong="H5186"\w* \w their ear|strong="H241"\w*.
\p \v 15 \w Recently|strong="H3117"\w* \w you|strong="H859"\w* \w repented|strong="H7725"\w* \w and did|strong="H6213"\w* \w what pleased|strong="H3477"\w* \w Me|strong="H5869"\w*; \w each|strong="H376"\w* \w of you proclaimed|strong="H7121"\w* \w freedom|strong="H1865"\w* \w for his neighbor|strong="H7453"\w*. \w You made|strong="H3772"\w* \w a covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w before Me|strong="H6440"\w* \w in the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w bears|strong="H7121"\w* \w My Name|strong="H8034"\w*. \v 16 \w But now you have changed your minds|strong="H7725"\w* \w and profaned|strong="H2490"\w* \w My name|strong="H8034"\w*. \w Each of you|strong="H376"\w* \w has taken back|strong="H7725"\w* \w the menservants and maidservants|strong="H5650"\w* \w whom|strong="H834"\w* \w you had set|strong="H7971"\w* \w at liberty|strong="H2670"\w* \w to go wherever they wanted|strong="H5315"\w*, \w and you have again forced|strong="H3533"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w to be|strong="H1961"\w* your \w slaves|strong="H5650"\w*.
\p \v 17 \w Therefore|strong="H3651"\w* \w this is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w You|strong="H859"\w* \w have not|strong="H3808"\w* \w obeyed|strong="H8085"\w* \w Me|strong="H413"\w*; \w you have not proclaimed|strong="H7121"\w* \w freedom|strong="H1865"\w*, \w each man|strong="H376"\w* \w for his brother|strong="H251"\w* \w and for his neighbor|strong="H7453"\w*. \w So now|strong="H2005"\w* \w I proclaim|strong="H7121"\w* \w freedom|strong="H1865"\w* for you, \w declares|strong="H5002"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* — \w freedom to fall|strong="H413"\w* \w by sword|strong="H2719"\w*, \w by|strong="H413"\w* \w plague|strong="H1698"\w*, \w and by|strong="H413"\w* \w famine|strong="H7458"\w*! \w I will make you|strong="H5414"\w* \w a horror|strong="H2113"\w* \w to all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the kingdoms|strong="H4467"\w* \w of the earth|strong="H776"\w*.
\p \v 18 \w And those who have transgressed|strong="H5674"\w* \w My covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w and have not|strong="H3808"\w* \w fulfilled|strong="H6965"\w* \w the terms|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the covenant|strong="H1285"\w* \w they made|strong="H3772"\w* \w before Me|strong="H6440"\w*, \w I will treat|strong="H5414"\w* \w like the calf|strong="H5695"\w* \w they cut|strong="H3772"\w* \w in two|strong="H8147"\w* \w in order to pass|strong="H5674"\w* \w between|strong="H996"\w* \w its pieces|strong="H1335"\w*. \v 19 \w The officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w and Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*, \w the court officials|strong="H5631"\w*, \w the priests|strong="H3548"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w who passed|strong="H5674"\w* \w between|strong="H996"\w* \w the pieces|strong="H1335"\w* \w of the calf|strong="H5695"\w*, \v 20 \w I will deliver|strong="H5414"\w* \w into the hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w of their enemies|strong="H341"\w* \w who seek|strong="H1245"\w* \w their lives|strong="H5315"\w*. \w Their corpses|strong="H5038"\w* \w will become|strong="H1961"\w* \w food|strong="H3978"\w* \w for the birds|strong="H5775"\w* \w of the air|strong="H8064"\w* \w and the beasts|strong="H929"\w* \w of the earth|strong="H776"\w*. \v 21 \w And|strong="H853"\w* \w I will deliver|strong="H5414"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w and his officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w into the hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w of their enemies|strong="H341"\w* \w who seek|strong="H1245"\w* \w their lives|strong="H5315"\w*, \w to the army|strong="H2428"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w that had withdrawn|strong="H5927"\w* \w from you|strong="H5921"\w*.
\p \v 22 \w Behold|strong="H2005"\w*, \w I am going to give the command|strong="H6680"\w*, \w declares|strong="H5002"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w and I will bring them back|strong="H7725"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w*. \w They will fight|strong="H3898"\w* \w against it|strong="H5921"\w*, \w capture it|strong="H3920"\w*, \w and burn it down|strong="H8313"\w*. \w And|strong="H853"\w* \w I will make|strong="H5414"\w* \w the cities|strong="H5892"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w a desolation|strong="H8077"\w*, \w without|strong="H369"\w* \w inhabitant|strong="H3427"\w*.”
\c 35
\s1 The Obedience of the Rechabites
\p \v 1 \w This is the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w from the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w in the days|strong="H3117"\w* \w of Jehoiakim|strong="H3079"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Josiah|strong="H2977"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*: \v 2 “\w Go|strong="H1980"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the Rechabites|strong="H7397"\w*, \w speak|strong="H1696"\w* \w to them|strong="H853"\w*, \w and bring them|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w one|strong="H259"\w* \w of the chambers|strong="H3957"\w* \w of the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w to offer them a drink|strong="H8248"\w* \w of wine|strong="H3196"\w*.”
\p \v 3 \w So I took|strong="H3947"\w* \w Jaazaniah|strong="H2970"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Habazziniah|strong="H2262"\w*, \w and his brothers|strong="H251"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w his sons|strong="H1121"\w*— \w the entire|strong="H3605"\w* \w house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the Rechabites|strong="H7397"\w*— \v 4 \w and I brought|strong="H935"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w into the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w a chamber|strong="H3957"\w* \w occupied by the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Hanan|strong="H2605"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Igdaliah|strong="H3012"\w*, \w a man|strong="H376"\w* \w of God|strong="H430"\w*. \w This room was|strong="H834"\w* \w near|strong="H681"\w* \w the chamber|strong="H3957"\w* \w of the officials|strong="H8269"\w*, \w which|strong="H834"\w* \w was above|strong="H4605"\w* \w the chamber|strong="H3957"\w* \w of Maaseiah|strong="H4641"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Shallum|strong="H7967"\w* \w the doorkeeper|strong="H8104"\w*.
\p \v 5 \w Then I set|strong="H5414"\w* \w pitchers|strong="H1375"\w* \w full|strong="H4392"\w* \w of wine|strong="H3196"\w* \w and some cups|strong="H3563"\w* \w before|strong="H6440"\w* \w the men|strong="H1121"\w* \w of the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the Rechabites|strong="H7397"\w*, \w and I said|strong="H559"\w* \w to them|strong="H413"\w*, “\w Drink|strong="H8354"\w* \w some wine|strong="H3196"\w*.”
\p \v 6 “\w We do not|strong="H3808"\w* \w drink|strong="H8354"\w* \w wine|strong="H3196"\w*,” \w they replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w our forefather|strong="H1"\w* \w Jonadab|strong="H3122"\w*\f + \fr 35:6 \fqa Jonadab \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehonadab\ft ; here and throughout this chapter; see \ref 2 Kings 10:15|2KI 10:15\ref*.\f* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Rechab|strong="H7394"\w* \w commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w us|strong="H5921"\w*, ‘\w Neither you|strong="H859"\w* \w nor your descendants|strong="H1121"\w* \w are ever to|strong="H3808"\w* \w drink|strong="H8354"\w* \w wine|strong="H3196"\w*. \v 7 \w Nor are you ever|strong="H3808"\w* \w to build|strong="H1129"\w* \w a house|strong="H1004"\w* \w or|strong="H3808"\w* \w sow|strong="H2232"\w* \w seed|strong="H2233"\w* \w or|strong="H3808"\w* \w plant|strong="H5193"\w* \w a vineyard|strong="H3754"\w*. \w Those things are|strong="H1961"\w* \w not|strong="H3808"\w* for you. \w Instead|strong="H3588"\w*, \w you must live|strong="H3427"\w* \w in tents|strong="H168"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w your lives|strong="H3117"\w*, \w so that|strong="H4616"\w* \w you may live|strong="H2421"\w* \w a long|strong="H7227"\w* \w time|strong="H3117"\w* \w in|strong="H5921"\w* \w the land|strong="H127"\w* \w where|strong="H834"\w* \w you|strong="H859"\w* \w wander|strong="H1481"\w*.’
\p \v 8 \w And we have obeyed|strong="H8085"\w* \w the voice|strong="H6963"\w* \w of our forefather|strong="H1"\w* \w Jonadab|strong="H3082"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Rechab|strong="H7394"\w* \w in all|strong="H3605"\w* \w he commanded us|strong="H6680"\w*. \w So we have not|strong="H1115"\w* \w drunk|strong="H8354"\w* \w wine|strong="H3196"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w our lives|strong="H3117"\w*— \w neither we|strong="H587"\w* \w nor our wives|strong="H802"\w* \w nor our sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w and daughters|strong="H1323"\w*. \v 9 \w Nor have we|strong="H1115"\w* \w built|strong="H1129"\w* \w houses|strong="H1004"\w* \w in which to live|strong="H3427"\w*, \w and we have not owned|strong="H1961"\w* \w any vineyards|strong="H3754"\w* \w or fields|strong="H7704"\w* \w or crops|strong="H2233"\w*. \v 10 \w But we have lived|strong="H3427"\w* \w in tents|strong="H168"\w* \w and have obeyed|strong="H8085"\w* \w and done|strong="H6213"\w* \w exactly as|strong="H3605"\w* \w our forefather|strong="H1"\w* \w Jonadab|strong="H3122"\w* \w commanded us|strong="H6680"\w*.
\p \v 11 \w So when|strong="H1961"\w* \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w marched|strong="H5927"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w the land|strong="H776"\w*, \w we said|strong="H559"\w*: ‘\w Come|strong="H935"\w*, \w let us go into|strong="H935"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w to escape|strong="H6440"\w* \w the armies|strong="H2428"\w* \w of the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*\f + \fr 35:11 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f* \w and the Arameans|strong="H758"\w*.’ \w So we have remained|strong="H3427"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*.”
\s1 Judah Rebuked
\p \v 12 \w Then the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w came|strong="H1961"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*: \v 13 “\w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H6635"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w Go|strong="H1980"\w* \w and tell|strong="H559"\w* \w the men|strong="H376"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w and the residents|strong="H3427"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*: ‘\w Will you not|strong="H3808"\w* \w accept|strong="H3947"\w* \w discipline|strong="H4148"\w* \w and obey|strong="H8085"\w* \w My words|strong="H1697"\w*?’ \w declares|strong="H5002"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*.
