\p \v 4 \w Now Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w was free to come|strong="H935"\w* \w and go|strong="H3318"\w* \w among|strong="H8432"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w for they had not|strong="H3808"\w* \w yet put|strong="H5414"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w in prison|strong="H1004"\w*. \v 5 \w Pharaoh’s|strong="H6547"\w* \w army|strong="H2428"\w* \w had left|strong="H3318"\w* \w Egypt|strong="H4714"\w*, \w and when the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*\f + \fr 37:5 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verses 8, 9, 13, and 14\f* \w who were besieging|strong="H6696"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w the report|strong="H8088"\w*, \w they withdrew|strong="H5927"\w* \w from|strong="H5921"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*.
