\p \v 9 \w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w deceive|strong="H5377"\w* \w yourselves|strong="H5315"\w* \w by saying|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w The Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w* \w will go away for good|strong="H1980"\w*,’ \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w they will not|strong="H3808"\w*! \v 10 \w Indeed|strong="H3588"\w*, \w if|strong="H518"\w* \w you were to strike down|strong="H5221"\w* \w the entire|strong="H3605"\w* \w army|strong="H2428"\w* \w of the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w* \w that is fighting|strong="H3898"\w* \w against you|strong="H854"\w*, \w and only wounded|strong="H1856"\w* \w men|strong="H582"\w* \w remained|strong="H7604"\w* \w in their tents|strong="H168"\w*, \w they would still get up|strong="H6965"\w* \w and burn this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w down|strong="H8313"\w*.”
\s1 Jeremiah Imprisoned
\p \v 11 \w When the Chaldean|strong="H3778"\w* \w army|strong="H2428"\w* \w withdrew|strong="H5927"\w* \w from|strong="H5921"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w for fear|strong="H6440"\w* \w of Pharaoh’s|strong="H6547"\w* \w army|strong="H2428"\w*, \v 12 \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w started to leave|strong="H3318"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w to go|strong="H1980"\w* \w to the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Benjamin|strong="H1144"\w* \w to claim his portion|strong="H2505"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*\f + \fr 37:12 \ft Literally \fqa to divide from there\f* \w among|strong="H8432"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*. \v 13 \w But when he|strong="H1931"\w* \w reached|strong="H1961"\w* \w the Gate|strong="H8179"\w* \w of Benjamin|strong="H1144"\w*, \w the captain|strong="H1167"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H6488"\w*, \w whose name|strong="H8034"\w* \w was Irijah|strong="H3376"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Shelemiah|strong="H8018"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Hananiah|strong="H2608"\w*, \w seized|strong="H8610"\w* \w him|strong="H3414"\w* \w and said|strong="H559"\w*, “\w You|strong="H859"\w* \w are deserting|strong="H5307"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*!”
\p \v 14 “\w That is a lie|strong="H8267"\w*,” \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*. “\w I am not|strong="H369"\w* \w deserting|strong="H5307"\w* \w to|strong="H5921"\w* \w the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*!”
\p \w But Irijah|strong="H3376"\w* \w would not|strong="H3808"\w* \w listen|strong="H8085"\w* \w to him|strong="H413"\w*; \w instead, he arrested|strong="H8610"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w and took him|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the officials|strong="H8269"\w*.
\p \v 15 \w The officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w were angry|strong="H7107"\w* \w with|strong="H5921"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*, \w and they beat|strong="H5221"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w and placed|strong="H5414"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w in jail|strong="H1004"\w* \w in the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of Jonathan|strong="H3083"\w* \w the scribe|strong="H5608"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w it had been made|strong="H6213"\w* \w into a prison|strong="H1004"\w*.
\p \v 16 \w So|strong="H3588"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w went|strong="H935"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w a cell|strong="H1004"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w the dungeon|strong="H2588"\w* \w and remained|strong="H3427"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w* \w a long time|strong="H7227"\w*.
\p \v 17 \w Later, King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w sent for Jeremiah|strong="H7971"\w* \w and received him|strong="H3947"\w* \w in his palace|strong="H1004"\w*, \w where he asked him|strong="H7592"\w* \w privately|strong="H5643"\w*, “\w Is there|strong="H3426"\w* \w a word|strong="H1697"\w* \w from the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*?”
\p “\w There is|strong="H3426"\w*,” \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*. “\w You will be delivered|strong="H5414"\w* \w into the hand|strong="H3027"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*.”
\p \v 18 \w Then Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w asked|strong="H559"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w*, “\w How|strong="H4100"\w* \w have I sinned|strong="H2398"\w* against you \w or your servants|strong="H5650"\w* \w or these|strong="H2088"\w* \w people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w you have put|strong="H5414"\w* \w me|strong="H853"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w prison|strong="H1004"\w*? \v 19 \w Where|strong="H335"\w* \w are your prophets|strong="H5030"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w prophesied|strong="H5012"\w* to you, \w claiming|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w The king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w come|strong="H935"\w* \w against you|strong="H5921"\w* \w or this|strong="H2063"\w* \w land|strong="H776"\w*’ ? \v 20 \w But now|strong="H6258"\w* \w please|strong="H4994"\w* \w listen|strong="H8085"\w*, \w O my lord|strong="H113"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*. \w May my petition|strong="H8467"\w* \w come|strong="H5307"\w* \w before you|strong="H6440"\w*. \w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w send me back|strong="H7725"\w* \w to the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of Jonathan|strong="H3083"\w* \w the scribe|strong="H5608"\w*, \w or|strong="H3808"\w* \w I will die|strong="H4191"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*.”
\p \v 21 \w So King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w gave orders|strong="H6680"\w* \w for Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w to be placed|strong="H6485"\w* \w in the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H4307"\w* \w and given|strong="H5414"\w* \w a loaf|strong="H3603"\w* \w of bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w daily|strong="H3117"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w the street|strong="H2351"\w* \w of the bakers|strong="H644"\w*, \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w in the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w was gone|strong="H8552"\w*. \w So Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w remained|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H4307"\w*.
\c 38
\s1 Jeremiah Cast into the Cistern
\p \v 1 \w Now Shephatiah|strong="H8203"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Mattan|strong="H4977"\w*, \w Gedaliah|strong="H1436"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Pashhur|strong="H6583"\w*, \w Jucal|strong="H3116"\w*\f + \fr 38:1 \fqa Jucal \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehucal\ft ; see \ref Jeremiah 37:3|JER 37:3\ref*.\f* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Shelemiah|strong="H8018"\w*, \w and Pashhur|strong="H6583"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Malchijah|strong="H4441"\w* \w heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w had been telling|strong="H1696"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*: \v 2 “\w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w Whoever stays|strong="H3427"\w* \w in this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w will die|strong="H4191"\w* \w by sword|strong="H2719"\w* \w and famine|strong="H7458"\w* \w and plague|strong="H1698"\w*, \w but whoever surrenders|strong="H3318"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*\f + \fr 38:2 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verses 18, 19, and 23\f* \w will live|strong="H2421"\w*; \w he will retain|strong="H1961"\w* \w his life|strong="H5315"\w* \w like a spoil of war|strong="H7998"\w*, \w and he will live|strong="H2421"\w*. \v 3 \w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w says|strong="H559"\w*: \w This|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w will surely be delivered|strong="H5414"\w* \w into the hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w of the army|strong="H2428"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w and he will capture it|strong="H3920"\w*.”
\p \v 4 \w Then the officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, “\w This|strong="H2088"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w* \w ought to die|strong="H4191"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w he|strong="H1931"\w* \w is discouraging|strong="H7503"\w* \w the warriors|strong="H582"\w* \w who remain|strong="H7604"\w* \w in this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w as well as all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w by speaking|strong="H1696"\w* \w such|strong="H428"\w* \w words|strong="H1697"\w* \w to them|strong="H413"\w*; \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w man|strong="H376"\w* \w is not|strong="H369"\w* \w seeking|strong="H1875"\w* \w the well-being|strong="H7965"\w* \w of these|strong="H2088"\w* \w people|strong="H5971"\w*, \w but|strong="H3588"\w* \w their ruin|strong="H7451"\w*.”
\p \v 5 “\w Here|strong="H2009"\w* \w he is|strong="H1931"\w*,” \w replied|strong="H559"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w*. “\w He is in your hands|strong="H3027"\w*, \w since|strong="H3588"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w can do nothing|strong="H369"\w* \w to stop you|strong="H1697"\w*.”
\p \v 6 \w So they took|strong="H3947"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w and dropped|strong="H7993"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w the cistern|strong="H953"\w* \w of Malchiah|strong="H4441"\w*, \w the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w*, \w which|strong="H834"\w* \w was in the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H4307"\w*. \w They lowered|strong="H7971"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w with ropes|strong="H2256"\w* \w into the cistern|strong="H953"\w*, \w which had no|strong="H369"\w* \w water|strong="H4325"\w* \w but only|strong="H3588"\w* \w mud|strong="H2916"\w*, \w and Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w sank down|strong="H2883"\w* \w into the mud|strong="H2916"\w*.
\p \v 7 \w Now Ebed-melech|strong="H5663"\w* \w the Cushite|strong="H3569"\w*,\f + \fr 38:7 \ft Probably from the upper Nile region\f* \w a court official|strong="H5631"\w*\f + \fr 38:7 \ft Or \fqa eunuch\f* \w in the royal|strong="H4428"\w* \w palace|strong="H1004"\w*, \w heard|strong="H8085"\w* \w that Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w had been put|strong="H5414"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w the cistern|strong="H953"\w*. \w While the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w was sitting|strong="H3427"\w* \w at the Gate|strong="H8179"\w* \w of Benjamin|strong="H1144"\w*, \v 8 \w Ebed-melech|strong="H5663"\w* \w went out|strong="H3318"\w* \w from the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w palace|strong="H1004"\w* \w and said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \v 9 “\w My lord|strong="H113"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w*, \w these|strong="H428"\w* \w men|strong="H582"\w* \w have acted wickedly|strong="H7489"\w* \w in all|strong="H3605"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w they have done|strong="H6213"\w* \w to Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H5030"\w*. \w They have dropped him|strong="H7993"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w the cistern|strong="H953"\w*, \w where|strong="H8478"\w* \w he will starve to death|strong="H4191"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w there is no|strong="H369"\w* \w more|strong="H5750"\w* \w bread|strong="H3899"\w* \w in the city|strong="H5892"\w*.”
\p \v 10 \w So the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w commanded|strong="H6680"\w* \w Ebed-melech|strong="H5663"\w* \w the Cushite|strong="H3569"\w*, “\w Take|strong="H3947"\w* \w thirty|strong="H7970"\w* \w men|strong="H582"\w* \w from|strong="H4480"\w* \w here|strong="H2088"\w* \w with you|strong="H3027"\w* \w and pull|strong="H5927"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w out of the cistern|strong="H953"\w* \w before|strong="H2962"\w* \w he dies|strong="H4191"\w*.”
\p \v 11 \w Then Ebed-melech|strong="H5663"\w* \w took|strong="H3947"\w* \w the men|strong="H582"\w* \w with him|strong="H3027"\w* \w and went|strong="H935"\w* \w to the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w palace|strong="H1004"\w*, \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w a place below|strong="H8478"\w* \w the storehouse|strong="H214"\w*. \w From there|strong="H8033"\w* \w he took|strong="H3947"\w* \w old|strong="H1094"\w* \w rags|strong="H5499"\w* \w and worn-out|strong="H1094"\w* \w clothes|strong="H4418"\w* \w and lowered them|strong="H7971"\w* \w with ropes|strong="H2256"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w in|strong="H413"\w* \w the cistern|strong="H953"\w*.
\p \v 12 \w Ebed-melech|strong="H5663"\w* \w the Cushite|strong="H3569"\w* \w cried out|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*, “\w Put|strong="H7760"\w* \w these worn-out|strong="H1094"\w* \w rags|strong="H5499"\w* \w and clothes|strong="H4418"\w* \w under your arms|strong="H679"\w* \w to pad the ropes|strong="H2256"\w*.” \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w did|strong="H6213"\w* \w so|strong="H3651"\w*, \v 13 \w and they pulled him|strong="H3414"\w* \w up|strong="H4900"\w* \w with the ropes|strong="H2256"\w* \w and lifted|strong="H5927"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w out of|strong="H4480"\w* \w the cistern|strong="H953"\w*. \w And Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w remained|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H4307"\w*.
\p \v 14 \w Then King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w sent for|strong="H7971"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w and received|strong="H3947"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w at|strong="H413"\w* \w the third|strong="H7992"\w* \w entrance|strong="H3996"\w* \w to the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*. “\w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am going to ask|strong="H7592"\w* \w you something|strong="H1697"\w*,” \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*. “\w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w hide|strong="H3582"\w* \w anything|strong="H1697"\w* \w from me|strong="H4480"\w*.”
\p \v 15 “\w If|strong="H3588"\w* \w I tell you|strong="H5046"\w*,” \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*, “\w you will surely put me to death|strong="H4191"\w*. \w And even if|strong="H3588"\w* \w I give you advice|strong="H3289"\w*, \w you will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w listen|strong="H8085"\w* \w to me|strong="H413"\w*.”
\p \v 16 \w But King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w swore|strong="H7650"\w* \w secretly|strong="H5643"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*, “\w As surely as the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w lives|strong="H2416"\w*, \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w has given|strong="H6213"\w* us \w this|strong="H2063"\w* \w life|strong="H5315"\w*, \w I will not|strong="H518"\w* \w kill you|strong="H4191"\w*, \w nor|strong="H518"\w* \w will I deliver you|strong="H5414"\w* \w into the hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w of these|strong="H428"\w* \w men|strong="H582"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w are seeking|strong="H1245"\w* \w your life|strong="H5315"\w*.”
\p \v 17 \w Then Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w*, “\w This is what|strong="H3541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H6635"\w*, \w the God|strong="H430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H3478"\w*, \w says|strong="H559"\w*: ‘\w If|strong="H518"\w* \w you indeed surrender|strong="H3318"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the officers|strong="H8269"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w then you|strong="H5315"\w* \w will live|strong="H2421"\w*, \w this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w be burned down|strong="H8313"\w*, \w and you|strong="H859"\w* \w and your household|strong="H1004"\w* \w will survive|strong="H2421"\w*. \v 18 \w But if|strong="H518"\w* \w you do not|strong="H3808"\w* \w surrender|strong="H3318"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the officers|strong="H8269"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w then this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w will be delivered|strong="H5414"\w* \w into the hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w of the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*. \w They will burn it down|strong="H8313"\w*, \w and you|strong="H859"\w* \w yourself will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w escape|strong="H4422"\w* \w their grasp|strong="H3027"\w*.’”
\p \v 19 \w But King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*, “\w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am afraid|strong="H1672"\w* \w of the Jews|strong="H3064"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w have deserted|strong="H5307"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*, \w for the Chaldeans|strong="H6435"\w* \w may deliver|strong="H5414"\w* \w me|strong="H853"\w* \w into their hands|strong="H3027"\w* \w to abuse|strong="H5953"\w* me.”
\p \v 20 “\w They will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w hand you over|strong="H5414"\w*,” \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w replied|strong="H559"\w*. “\w Obey|strong="H8085"\w* \w the voice|strong="H6963"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w in what|strong="H834"\w* \w I|strong="H589"\w* \w am telling you|strong="H1696"\w*, \w that it may go well|strong="H3190"\w* with you \w and you|strong="H5315"\w* \w may live|strong="H2421"\w*. \v 21 \w But if|strong="H518"\w* \w you|strong="H859"\w* \w refuse|strong="H3986"\w* \w to surrender|strong="H3318"\w*, \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w is the word|strong="H1697"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H3068"\w* \w has shown me|strong="H7200"\w*: \v 22 \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w the women|strong="H802"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w remain|strong="H7604"\w* \w in the palace|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w will be brought out|strong="H3318"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w and those women|strong="H2007"\w* \w will say|strong="H559"\w*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\w They misled you|strong="H5496"\w* \w and overcame|strong="H3201"\w* you —
\q2 \w those trusted|strong="H7965"\w* \w friends of yours|strong="H582"\w*.
\q1 \w Your feet|strong="H7272"\w* \w sank|strong="H2883"\w* \w into the mire|strong="H1206"\w*,
\q2 \w and they deserted|strong="H5472"\w* \w you|strong="H268"\w*.’
\p \v 23 \w All|strong="H3605"\w* \w your wives|strong="H802"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w children|strong="H1121"\w* \w will be brought out|strong="H3318"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*. \w And you|strong="H859"\w* \w yourself will not|strong="H3808"\w* \w escape|strong="H4422"\w* \w their grasp|strong="H3027"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w you will be seized|strong="H8610"\w* \w by|strong="H3027"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w and this|strong="H2063"\w* \w city|strong="H5892"\w* \w will be burned down|strong="H8313"\w*.”
\p \v 24 \w Then Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w warned|strong="H559"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*, “\w Do not|strong="H408"\w* \w let anyone|strong="H376"\w* \w know|strong="H3045"\w* \w about this|strong="H428"\w* \w conversation|strong="H1697"\w*, \w or|strong="H3808"\w* \w you will die|strong="H4191"\w*. \v 25 \w If|strong="H3588"\w* \w the officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w hear|strong="H8085"\w* \w that|strong="H3588"\w* \w I have spoken|strong="H1696"\w* \w with you|strong="H854"\w*, \w and they come|strong="H935"\w* \w and demand|strong="H559"\w* \w of you|strong="H413"\w*, ‘\w Tell|strong="H5046"\w* us \w what|strong="H4100"\w* \w you said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and what|strong="H4100"\w* \w he|strong="H4428"\w* \w said|strong="H1696"\w* \w to you|strong="H413"\w*; \w do not|strong="H408"\w* \w hide it|strong="H3582"\w* \w from us|strong="H4480"\w*, \w or|strong="H3808"\w* \w we will kill you|strong="H4191"\w*,’ \v 26 \w then tell them|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w I|strong="H589"\w* \w was presenting|strong="H5307"\w* \w to|strong="H6440"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w my petition|strong="H8467"\w* \w that he not|strong="H1115"\w* \w return me|strong="H7725"\w* \w to the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of Jonathan|strong="H3083"\w* \w to die|strong="H4191"\w* \w there|strong="H8033"\w*.’”
\p \v 27 \w When all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w came|strong="H935"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w and questioned him|strong="H7592"\w*, \w he relayed|strong="H5046"\w* to them \w the exact|strong="H3605"\w* \w words|strong="H1697"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w had commanded him to say|strong="H6680"\w*. \w So they said no more|strong="H2790"\w* \w to him|strong="H4480"\w*, \w for|strong="H3588"\w* \w no one|strong="H3808"\w* \w had overheard|strong="H8085"\w* \w the conversation|strong="H1697"\w*. \v 28 \w And Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w remained|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the courtyard|strong="H2691"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H4307"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w the day|strong="H3117"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w was captured|strong="H3920"\w*.
\c 39
\s1 The Fall of Jerusalem
\r (\ref 2 Kings 25:1–12|2KI 25:1-12\ref*; \ref 2 Chronicles 36:15–21|2CH 36:15-21\ref*)
\p \v 1 \w In the ninth|strong="H8671"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*, \w in the tenth|strong="H6224"\w* \w month|strong="H2320"\w*, \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w marched|strong="H935"\w* \w against|strong="H413"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w with his entire|strong="H3605"\w* \w army|strong="H2428"\w* \w and laid siege|strong="H6696"\w* \w to the city|strong="H5921"\w*. \v 2 \w And on the ninth|strong="H8672"\w* \w day|strong="H2320"\w* \w of the fourth|strong="H7243"\w* \w month|strong="H2320"\w* \w of Zedekiah’s|strong="H6667"\w* \w eleventh|strong="H6249"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w*, \w the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w was breached|strong="H1234"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w Then all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w entered|strong="H935"\w* \w and sat|strong="H3427"\w* \w in the Middle|strong="H8432"\w* \w Gate|strong="H8179"\w*: \w Nergal-sharezer|strong="H5371"\w* \w of Samgar|strong="H5562"\w*, \w Nebo-sarsekim|strong="H8310"\w*\f + \fr 39:3 \ft Or \fqa Nergal-sharezer, Samgar-nebo, Sarsekim\f* \w the Rabsaris|strong="H7249"\w*,\f + \fr 39:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa Rabsaris \ft is the title of the chief eunuch in the Assyrian military; also in verse 13.\f* \w Nergal-sharezer|strong="H5371"\w* \w the Rabmag|strong="H7248"\w*,\f + \fr 39:3 \ft Hebrew \fqa Rabmag \ft is the title of the chief soothsayer or chief of princes in the Assyrian military; also in verse 13.\f* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the rest|strong="H7611"\w* \w of the officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*.
\p \v 4 \w When|strong="H834"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the soldiers|strong="H582"\w* \w saw them|strong="H7200"\w*, \w they fled|strong="H1272"\w*. \w They left|strong="H3318"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w at night|strong="H3915"\w* \w by way|strong="H1870"\w* \w of the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w garden|strong="H1588"\w*, \w through the gate|strong="H8179"\w* \w between|strong="H996"\w* \w the two walls|strong="H2346"\w*, \w and they went out|strong="H3318"\w* \w along the route|strong="H1870"\w* \w to the Arabah|strong="H6160"\w*.\f + \fr 39:4 \ft Or \fqa the Jordan Valley\f* \v 5 \w But the army|strong="H2428"\w* \w of the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*\f + \fr 39:5 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verse 8\f* \w pursued|strong="H7291"\w* \w them|strong="H310"\w* \w and overtook|strong="H5381"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w in the plains|strong="H6160"\w* \w of Jericho|strong="H3405"\w*. \w They seized|strong="H3947"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w and brought him up|strong="H5927"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w at Riblah|strong="H7247"\w* \w in the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Hamath|strong="H2574"\w*, \w where he pronounced|strong="H1696"\w* \w judgment|strong="H4941"\w* \w on him|strong="H854"\w*.
\p \v 6 \w There at Riblah|strong="H7247"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w slaughtered|strong="H7819"\w* \w the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w before his eyes|strong="H5869"\w*, \w and he|strong="H4428"\w* \w also killed|strong="H7819"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the nobles|strong="H2715"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*. \v 7 \w Then he put out|strong="H5786"\w* \w Zedekiah’s|strong="H6667"\w* \w eyes|strong="H5869"\w* \w and bound him|strong="H631"\w* \w with bronze chains|strong="H5178"\w* \w to take|strong="H935"\w* \w him|strong="H853"\w* \w to Babylon|strong="H894"\w*.
