\s1 Jeremiah’s Message to Seraiah
\p \v 59 \w This is the message|strong="H1697"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w the prophet|strong="H5030"\w* \w gave|strong="H6680"\w* \w to the quartermaster|strong="H4496"\w* \w Seraiah|strong="H8304"\w* \w son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Neriah|strong="H5374"\w*, \w the son|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Mahseiah|strong="H4271"\w*, \w when he went|strong="H1980"\w* \w to Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w with|strong="H854"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w* \w in the fourth|strong="H7243"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of Zedekiah’s reign|strong="H4427"\w*. \v 60 \w Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w had written|strong="H3789"\w* \w on|strong="H413"\w* \w a single|strong="H259"\w* \w scroll|strong="H5612"\w* \w about all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the disaster|strong="H7451"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w would come|strong="H935"\w* \w upon|strong="H413"\w* \w Babylon|strong="H894"\w* — \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w these|strong="H428"\w* \w words|strong="H1697"\w* \w that had been written|strong="H3789"\w* \w concerning|strong="H413"\w* \w Babylon|strong="H894"\w*.
\p \v 61 \w And Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w* \w said|strong="H559"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w Seraiah|strong="H8304"\w*, “\w When you get|strong="H935"\w* \w to Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w see|strong="H7200"\w* \w that you read all|strong="H3605"\w* \w these|strong="H428"\w* \w words|strong="H1697"\w* \w aloud|strong="H7121"\w*, \v 62 \w and say|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w O LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w You|strong="H859"\w* \w have promised|strong="H1696"\w* \w to cut off|strong="H3772"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w place|strong="H4725"\w* \w so that no one|strong="H1115"\w* \w will remain|strong="H3427"\w* — \w neither man|strong="H120"\w* \w nor|strong="H5704"\w* \w beast|strong="H929"\w*. \w Indeed|strong="H3588"\w*, \w it will be|strong="H1961"\w* \w desolate|strong="H8077"\w* \w forever|strong="H5769"\w*.’
\p \v 63 \w When you finish|strong="H3615"\w* \w reading|strong="H7121"\w* \w this|strong="H2088"\w* \w scroll|strong="H5612"\w*, \w tie|strong="H7194"\w* \w a stone|strong="H68"\w* \w to it|strong="H5921"\w* \w and cast it|strong="H7993"\w* \w into|strong="H413"\w* \w the Euphrates|strong="H6578"\w*. \v 64 \w Then you are to say|strong="H559"\w*, ‘\w In the same way|strong="H3602"\w* \w Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w will sink|strong="H8257"\w* \w and never|strong="H3808"\w* \w rise again|strong="H6965"\w*, \w because of|strong="H6440"\w* \w the disaster|strong="H7451"\w* \w I|strong="H595"\w* \w will bring|strong="H935"\w* \w upon her|strong="H5921"\w*. \w And her people will grow weary|strong="H3286"\w*.’”
\p \w Here|strong="H2008"\w* \w end|strong="H5704"\w* \w the words|strong="H1697"\w* \w of Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*.
\c 52
\s1 The Fall of Jerusalem Recounted
\r (\ref Psalm 74:1–23|PSA 74:1-23\ref*; \ref Psalm 79:1–13|PSA 79:1-13\ref*; \ref 2 Kings 24:18–20|2KI 24:18-20\ref*; \ref 2 Chronicles 36:11–14|2CH 36:11-14\ref*)
\p \v 1 \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w was twenty-one|strong="H6242"\w* \w years|strong="H8141"\w* \w old|strong="H1121"\w* \w when he became king|strong="H4427"\w*, \w and he reigned|strong="H4427"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w eleven|strong="H259"\w* \w years|strong="H8141"\w*. \w His mother’s|strong="H517"\w* \w name|strong="H8034"\w* \w was Hamutal|strong="H2537"\w* \w daughter|strong="H1323"\w* \w of Jeremiah|strong="H3414"\w*; \w she was from Libnah|strong="H3841"\w*.
\p \v 2 \w And Zedekiah did|strong="H6213"\w* \w evil|strong="H7451"\w* \w in the sight|strong="H5869"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w just as|strong="H3605"\w* \w Jehoiakim|strong="H3079"\w* \w had done|strong="H6213"\w*. \v 3 \w For|strong="H3588"\w* \w because|strong="H5921"\w* \w of the anger|strong="H639"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w all this happened|strong="H1961"\w* \w in Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w and Judah|strong="H3063"\w*, \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w He finally banished|strong="H7993"\w* \w them|strong="H853"\w* \w from|strong="H5921"\w* \w His presence|strong="H6440"\w*.
\p \w And Zedekiah also|strong="H6667"\w* \w rebelled|strong="H4775"\w* \w against the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*.
\p \v 4 \w So|strong="H1961"\w* \w in the ninth|strong="H8671"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of Zedekiah’s reign|strong="H4427"\w*, \w on the tenth|strong="H6218"\w* \w day of the tenth|strong="H6224"\w* \w month|strong="H2320"\w*, \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H5019"\w* \w king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w marched|strong="H935"\w* \w against|strong="H5921"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* \w with his entire|strong="H3605"\w* \w army|strong="H2428"\w*. \w They encamped|strong="H2583"\w* \w outside the city|strong="H5921"\w* \w and built|strong="H1129"\w* \w a siege wall|strong="H1785"\w* \w all|strong="H5439"\w* \w around it|strong="H5921"\w*. \v 5 \w And the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w was kept|strong="H935"\w* \w under siege|strong="H4692"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Zedekiah’s|strong="H6667"\w* \w eleventh|strong="H6249"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w*.
\p \v 6 \w By the ninth day|strong="H8672"\w* \w of the fourth|strong="H7243"\w* \w month|strong="H2320"\w*, \w the famine|strong="H7458"\w* \w in the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w was so severe|strong="H2388"\w* \w that the people|strong="H5971"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w had|strong="H1961"\w* \w no|strong="H3808"\w* \w food|strong="H3899"\w*. \v 7 \w Then the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w was breached|strong="H1234"\w*; \w and though the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w*\f + \fr 52:7 \ft That is, the Babylonians; similarly in verses 8, 9, 14, and 17 \f* \w had surrounded|strong="H5439"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the men|strong="H582"\w* \w of war|strong="H4421"\w* \w fled|strong="H1272"\w* \w the city|strong="H5892"\w* \w by night|strong="H3915"\w* \w by way|strong="H1870"\w* \w of the gate|strong="H8179"\w* \w between|strong="H996"\w* \w the two walls|strong="H2346"\w* \w near|strong="H5921"\w* \w the king’s|strong="H4428"\w* \w garden|strong="H1588"\w*.
\p \w They headed|strong="H1980"\w* \w toward|strong="H1870"\w* \w the Arabah|strong="H6160"\w*,\f + \fr 52:7 \ft Or \fqa the Jordan Valley\f* \v 8 \w but the army|strong="H2428"\w* \w of the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w* \w pursued|strong="H7291"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and overtook|strong="H5381"\w* \w Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w in the plains|strong="H6160"\w* \w of Jericho|strong="H3405"\w*, \w and his whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w army|strong="H2428"\w* \w deserted|strong="H6327"\w* \w him|strong="H5921"\w*.
\p \v 9 \w The Chaldeans seized|strong="H8610"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w and brought him up|strong="H5927"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w at Riblah|strong="H7247"\w* \w in the land|strong="H776"\w* \w of Hamath|strong="H2574"\w*, \w where he pronounced|strong="H1696"\w* \w judgment|strong="H4941"\w* \w on Zedekiah|strong="H854"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w There at Riblah|strong="H7247"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w slaughtered|strong="H7819"\w* \w the sons|strong="H1121"\w* \w of Zedekiah|strong="H6667"\w* \w before his eyes|strong="H5869"\w*, \w and he also|strong="H1571"\w* \w killed|strong="H7819"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the officials|strong="H8269"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H3063"\w*. \v 11 \w Then he put out|strong="H5786"\w* \w Zedekiah’s|strong="H6667"\w* \w eyes|strong="H5869"\w*, \w bound|strong="H631"\w* \w him|strong="H4428"\w* \w with bronze shackles|strong="H5178"\w*, \w and took him|strong="H935"\w* \w to Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w where|strong="H894"\w* \w he kept him|strong="H5414"\w* \w in custody|strong="H1004"\w* \w until|strong="H5704"\w* \w his dying|strong="H4194"\w* \w day|strong="H3117"\w*.
\s1 The Temple Destroyed
\r (\ref 2 Kings 25:8–17|2KI 25:8-17\ref*)
\p \v 12 \w On the tenth|strong="H6218"\w* \w day of the fifth|strong="H2549"\w* \w month|strong="H2320"\w*, \w in the nineteenth|strong="H8672"\w* \w year|strong="H8141"\w* \w of Nebuchadnezzar’s|strong="H5019"\w* \w reign|strong="H4428"\w* \w over Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w Nebuzaradan|strong="H5018"\w* \w captain|strong="H7227"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H2876"\w*, \w a servant|strong="H5975"\w* \w of the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w*, \w entered|strong="H935"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*. \v 13 \w He burned down|strong="H8313"\w* \w the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the royal|strong="H4428"\w* \w palace|strong="H1004"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the houses|strong="H1004"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w* — \w every|strong="H3605"\w* \w significant|strong="H1419"\w* \w building|strong="H1004"\w*. \v 14 \w And|strong="H853"\w* \w the whole|strong="H3605"\w* \w army|strong="H2428"\w* \w of the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w* \w under|strong="H854"\w* \w the captain|strong="H7227"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H2876"\w* \w broke down|strong="H5422"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the walls|strong="H2346"\w* \w around|strong="H5439"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H3389"\w*.
\p \v 15 \w Then Nebuzaradan|strong="H5018"\w* \w captain|strong="H7227"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H2876"\w* \w carried into exile|strong="H1540"\w* \w some of the poorest|strong="H1803"\w* \w people|strong="H5971"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w those who remained|strong="H3499"\w* \w in the city|strong="H5892"\w*, \w along with|strong="H853"\w* \w the deserters|strong="H5307"\w* \w who|strong="H834"\w* \w had defected|strong="H5307"\w* \w to|strong="H413"\w* \w the king|strong="H4428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H894"\w* \w and the rest|strong="H3499"\w* \w of the craftsmen|strong="H525"\w*. \v 16 \w But Nebuzaradan|strong="H5018"\w* \w captain|strong="H7227"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H2876"\w* \w left behind|strong="H7604"\w* \w some of the poorest|strong="H1803"\w* \w of the land|strong="H776"\w* \w to tend the vineyards|strong="H3755"\w* \w and fields|strong="H3009"\w*.
\p \v 17 \w Moreover|strong="H853"\w*, \w the Chaldeans|strong="H3778"\w* \w broke up|strong="H7665"\w* \w the bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w pillars|strong="H5982"\w* \w and|strong="H853"\w* \w stands|strong="H4350"\w* \w and the bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w Sea|strong="H3220"\w* \w in the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w and they carried|strong="H5375"\w* \w all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w to Babylon|strong="H894"\w*. \v 18 \w They also|strong="H853"\w* \w took away|strong="H3947"\w* \w the pots|strong="H5518"\w*, \w shovels|strong="H3257"\w*, \w wick trimmers|strong="H4212"\w*, \w sprinkling bowls|strong="H4219"\w*, \w dishes|strong="H3709"\w*, \w and all|strong="H3605"\w* \w the articles|strong="H3627"\w* \w of bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w used in the temple service|strong="H8334"\w*. \v 19 \w The captain|strong="H7227"\w* \w of the guard|strong="H2876"\w* \w also took away|strong="H3947"\w* \w the basins|strong="H5592"\w*, \w censers|strong="H4289"\w*, \w sprinkling bowls|strong="H4219"\w*, \w pots|strong="H5518"\w*, \w lampstands|strong="H4501"\w*, \w pans|strong="H3709"\w*, \w and drink offering bowls|strong="H4518"\w*— \w anything made of|strong="H834"\w* \w pure gold|strong="H2091"\w* \w or fine silver|strong="H3701"\w*.
\p \v 20 \w As for the two|strong="H8147"\w* \w pillars|strong="H5982"\w*, \w the|strong="H259"\w* \w Sea|strong="H3220"\w*, \w the twelve|strong="H8147"\w* \w bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w bulls|strong="H1241"\w* \w under it|strong="H8478"\w*, \w and the movable stands|strong="H4350"\w* \w that|strong="H834"\w* \w King|strong="H4428"\w* \w Solomon|strong="H8010"\w* \w had made|strong="H6213"\w* \w for the house|strong="H1004"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H3068"\w*, \w the weight|strong="H4948"\w* \w of the bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w from all|strong="H3605"\w* \w these|strong="H428"\w* \w articles|strong="H3627"\w* \w was beyond measure|strong="H1961"\w*. \v 21 \w Each|strong="H259"\w* \w pillar|strong="H5982"\w* \w was eighteen|strong="H8083"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w tall|strong="H6967"\w* \w and twelve|strong="H8147"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w in circumference|strong="H5437"\w*;\f + \fr 52:21 \ft Each pillar was approximately 27 feet high and 18 feet in circumference (8.2 meters high and 5.5 meters in circumference).\f* \w each was hollow|strong="H5014"\w*, \w four|strong="H702"\w* \w fingers|strong="H676"\w* \w thick|strong="H5672"\w*.\f + \fr 52:21 \fqa 4 fingers \ft is approximately 2.9 inches or 7.4 centimeters.\f* \v 22 \w The bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w capital|strong="H3805"\w* \w atop|strong="H5921"\w* \w one pillar|strong="H259"\w* \w was five|strong="H2568"\w* \w cubits|strong="H520"\w* \w high|strong="H6967"\w*,\f + \fr 52:22 \fqa 5 cubits \ft is approximately 7.5 feet or 2.3 meters.\f* \w with a network|strong="H7639"\w* \w of bronze|strong="H5178"\w* \w pomegranates|strong="H7416"\w* \w all around|strong="H5439"\w*. \w The second|strong="H8145"\w* \w pillar|strong="H5982"\w*, \w with its pomegranates|strong="H7416"\w*, \w was similar|strong="H428"\w*. \v 23 \w Each capital had|strong="H1961"\w* \w ninety-six|strong="H8673"\w* \w pomegranates|strong="H7416"\w* \w on the sides|strong="H7307"\w*, \w and a total of|strong="H3605"\w* \w a hundred